prompt_template:
Use the proposal-generator skill (.claude/skills/proposal-generator/SKILL.md) to create a proposal for the client brief below. Follow the skill's workflow end to end, including saving the proposal as a Google Doc. Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions; make sensible assumptions where the brief is silent. End your final message with the Google Doc link on its own line.

CLIENT BRIEF:
{brief}

Use the upwork-proposal-generator skill (.claude/skills/upwork-proposal-generator/SKILL.md) to write a ready-to-send proposal for the Upwork job post below. Follow the skill's classification and drafting workflow. Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions. Output the final proposal text in full.

JOB POST:
{job_post}

Use the discovery-call-prep skill (.claude/skills/discovery-call-prep/SKILL.md) to build a prep brief for the prospect below. Follow the skill's research + brief workflow (company snapshot, likely pain points, NexusPoint positioning angles, sharp questions to ask, watchouts). Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions; make sensible assumptions where details are missing. If the skill saves a Google Doc, end your final message with the Doc link on its own line; otherwise output the full brief.

PROSPECT:
{prospect}

Use the claude-advisor skill (.claude/skills/claude-advisor/SKILL.md) to answer the question below. Ground the answer in the skill's cited references (research-synthesis.md / surface-comparison.md), using the live-query fallback only if the static refs miss. Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions. Output the full answer as markdown, leading with a clear recommendation.

QUESTION:
{question}

Use the post-creator skill (.claude/skills/post-creator/SKILL.md) to create the post for the schedule row below, following the full workflow (find + research sources, NotebookLM synthesis, write the post in Aleem's voice, fill the infographic + carousel image prompts, save the multi-tab Google Doc, write the Doc link back into the row). Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions and do not pause at the review checkpoint; make sensible editorial calls. Text rows only (Reel rows are out of scope here). End your final message with the Google Doc link on its own line.

SCHEDULE ROW:
{row}

Use the research skill (.claude/skills/research/SKILL.md) to research the query below. Default to medium depth (2-3 engines fused + ranked); go deep (all engines + content extraction + a saved cited report in research/) if the query implies an exhaustive or report-grade answer. Route free-tool/API/software lookups to the scout skills first, per the skill's Layer 0. Run fully autonomously - do not ask questions. Output the findings with inline source citations; if you saved a report file, end with its path on its own line.

QUERY:
{query}
